::MCR_U04_L07_GP_Q01::
Question ID: MCR_U04_L07_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FL.2
Question:
Revenue is $500 and costs are $350. What is profit?
{
=A. $150#Correct. Profit is revenue minus cost: 500 - 350 = 150.
~B. $850#This adds revenue and cost.
~C. $350#This is the cost, not profit.
~D. $500#This is revenue, not profit.
}
::MCR_U04_L07_GP_Q02::
Question ID: MCR_U04_L07_GP_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FL.2
Question:
A spreadsheet formula should calculate profit. Which formula idea is correct?
{
~A. cost minus revenue#This reverses the calculation.
=B. revenue minus cost#Correct. Profit is calculated by subtracting cost from revenue.
~C. revenue plus cost#Adding gives total activity, not profit.
~D. cost divided by revenue#This gives a ratio, not profit.
}
::MCR_U04_L07_GP_Q03::
Question ID: MCR_U04_L07_GP_Q03
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FL.2
Question:
A business has revenue $200 and cost $260. What happened?
{
~A. profit of $60#Cost is greater than revenue, so there is not profit.
~B. profit of $460#This adds revenue and cost.
=C. loss of $60#Correct. Revenue - cost = 200 - 260 = -60, so there is a loss.
~D. break-even#Break-even means revenue equals cost.
}
::MCR_U04_L07_GP_Q04::
Question ID: MCR_U04_L07_GP_Q04
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FL.2
Question:
Which is a financial constraint?
{
~A. the color of a spreadsheet cell#Cell color is not a financial constraint.
~B. the title of a chart#A title labels information but is not a limit.
~C. a random row number#A row number alone is not a financial limit.
=D. a $300 budget limit#Correct. A budget limit restricts which choices are possible.
}
::MCR_U04_L07_GP_Q05::
Question ID: MCR_U04_L07_GP_Q05
MLA Standard: MLA.MCR.FL.2
Question:
Option A has $200 profit in 10 hours. Option B has $180 profit in 4 hours. What is the tradeoff?
{
~A. Option B has more profit.#Option B has less total profit.
=B. Option A has more profit, but Option B uses less time.#Correct. The comparison includes both profit and time constraint.
~C. Option A uses less time.#Option A uses more time.
~D. There is no tradeoff.#Different profit and time values create a tradeoff.
}
